    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d271">

                <pb facs="0522" n="422" sameAs="frus:frus1880/pg422"/>

                <head>No. 271.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Evarts to Mr. White.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1880-04-14"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 14,
                        1880</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 96.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    dispatch No. 93 of the 4th ultimo, communicating the request of the committee of
                    the International Fishery Exhibition at Berlin, for the appointment of one or
                    two persons experienced in fishery matters as members of an international jury
                    which will be charged with reporting on the exhibits and awarding the
                    prizes.</p>
                <p>In reply I have to inform you that this Department has decided to designate
                    Deputy Commissioner George Brown Goode and Mr. Fred. <pb facs="0523" n="423"
                        xml:id="pg423"/> Mather, of his staff, to serve in the capacity indicated,
                    and you will accordingly notify the proper authorities of the exhibition to that
                    effect, and also inform the gentlemen just named of their designation.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>WM. M. EVARTS..</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
